@page "/projects/calico"

<PageTitle>Calico</PageTitle>

<div class="project-back">
    <NavLink class="project-back-link" href="/projects">
        &larr; Back to projects
    </NavLink>
</div>

<header class="project-detail-hero">
    <p class="project-type">Group project</p>
    <h1>Calico</h1>

    <p class="project-introduction">
        A LoFi music and productivity platform combining music discovery,
        playlist management and productivity tools in a Blazor application.
    </p>

    <ul class="project-technologies" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>C#</li>
        <li>ASP.NET Core</li>
        <li>Blazor</li>
        <li>Entity Framework Core</li>
        <li>Supabase</li>
        <li>YouTube API</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="project-actions">
        <a href="https://github.com/NC-Group1/lofi-backend"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Backend repository
        </a>

        <a href="https://github.com/NC-Group1/lofi-frontend"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Frontend repository
        </a>
    </div>
</header>

<section class="project-overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
    <div class="project-section-heading">
        <p class="project-section-label">Overview</p>
        <h2 id="overview-title">Combining music and productivity in one platform</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="project-section-content">
        <p>
            Calico was developed collaboratively as a full-stack group project,
            combining a Blazor frontend with an ASP.NET Core Web API.
        </p>
        <p>
            The platform brings together LoFi music discovery, playlists,
            project tracking and task-timer functionality in one application.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="project-contribution" aria-labelledby="contribution-title">
    <div class="project-section-heading">
        <p class="project-section-label">My contribution</p>
        <h2 id="contribution-title">Working within a collaborative development team</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="contribution-grid">
        <article class="contribution-card">
            <p class="contribution-label">Collaboration</p>
            <h3>Planning and delivering as a team</h3>
            <p>
                I worked primarily through pair programming, collaborating with and
                guiding teammates across frontend and backend tasks. We held daily
                stand-ups, managed our tasks with Trello and reviewed and merged our
                Git changes together at the end of each day.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="contribution-card">
            <p class="contribution-label">Individual work</p>
            <h3>Backend reliability and productivity features</h3>
            <p>
                Through pair programming, I contributed to layered user and task-timer
                functionality, including controller and service tests, and supported the
                YouTube API integration. Independently, I implemented the API and database
                health checks and developed the initial Pomodoro timer prototype.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="project-features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <div class="project-section-heading">
        <p class="project-section-label">Features</p>
        <h2 id="features-title">Music and productivity capabilities</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="features-list">
        <li>
            <span class="feature-number">01</span>
            <div>
                <h3>Music discovery and playback</h3>
                <p>Search for LoFi music and play embedded YouTube content.</p>
            </div>
        </li>

        <li>
            <span class="feature-number">02</span>
            <div>
                <h3>Playlist organisation</h3>
                <p>Create and manage playlists around selected music.</p>
            </div>
        </li>

        <li>
            <span class="feature-number">03</span>
            <div>
                <h3>Project and task tracking</h3>
                <p>Organise productivity work through projects and timed tasks.</p>
            </div>
        </li>

        <li>
            <span class="feature-number">04</span>
            <div>
                <h3>User accounts</h3>
                <p>Support registration, authentication and profile management.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="project-integrations" aria-labelledby="integrations-title">
    <div class="project-section-heading">
        <p class="project-section-label">Integrations</p>
        <h2 id="integrations-title">Connecting external services and application layers</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="integrations-grid">
        <article class="integration-card">
            <h3>Supabase authentication</h3>
            <p>
                User identity is integrated with Supabase and protected backend
                requests use authentication tokens.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="integration-card">
            <h3>YouTube media</h3>
            <p>
                YouTube content is incorporated into the music-discovery and
                playback experience.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="integration-card">
            <h3>Frontend and API communication</h3>
            <p>
                Blazor services use HTTP requests to exchange application data
                with the ASP.NET Core backend.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="project-reflection" aria-labelledby="reflection-title">
    <div class="reflection-content">
        <p class="project-section-label">Reflection</p>
        <h2 id="reflection-title">What I developed through collaborative work</h2>

        <p>
            Working on Calico strengthened my experience of pair programming,
            guiding teammates and contributing to a shared full-stack codebase.
            Daily stand-ups, Trello planning and collaborative Git reviews taught
            me how a development team coordinates work, shares knowledge and
            delivers features together.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-navigation">
        <NavLink class="project-navigation-link" href="/projects/recordshop">
            &larr; Previous project: RecordShop
        </NavLink>

        <NavLink class="project-navigation-link" href="/projects">
            All projects &rarr;
        </NavLink>
    </div>
</section>
